    "big": "Use an aquatic organism such as pondweed to investigate light intensity and photosynthesis rate. Change lamp distance or controlled illumination, measure time and oxygen output, and keep the same organism/length, CO₂ supply and temperature as constant as possible. Allow acclimatisation at each setting and take repeats.",
